2026-07-26T02:45:25.518695931Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: hey y'all
2026-07-26T02:45:25.518718232Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: okay we've put this off long enough. we keep saying our community has a certain way of doing things, and new folks have no way of knowing what that is. let's actually encode it.
2026-07-26T02:45:25.518733853Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: agreed, but carefully. I want this to help people understand our norms, not slap a scarlet letter on everyone who's new.
2026-07-26T02:45:25.518738463Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: two things I'd want marked. posts that fit our "from-scratch" ethos so people can find the good stuff. And the drive-by product spam that has nothing to do with our culture.
2026-07-26T02:45:25.518748194Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: yeah those are the two. one's a positive marker, one's a "this isn't us" marker.
2026-07-26T02:45:25.518764235Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: @CLEO can we get started?
2026-07-26T02:45:25.518841219Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [ai]: [{'text': 'Absolutely! Let\'s get started. I need to understand a bit more about your labeler\'s purpose before we design the labels.\n\n**What community is this for, and who\'s the intended audience?** \n\nI\'m picking up that you have a "from-scratch ethos" and want to help newcomers understand your norms while flagging product spam that doesn\'t fit your culture. But I need to know:\n\n- What kind of community is this? (e.g., a crafting community, a cooking community, a DIY/maker space, a gardening group?)\n- Who will subscribe to this labeler — just your community members, or are you hoping to help a broader audience find content that aligns with these values?\n\nThis context will help me design labels that truly serve your moderation goal and speak to your audience in the right way.', 'type': 'text', 'index': 0}]
2026-07-26T02:45:25.518870501Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: we're a home baking community of about 300 people on bluesky
2026-07-26T02:45:25.518887431Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: yea, our content is cnetered on home milling, naturally-leavened bread
2026-07-26T02:45:25.518894432Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: and sourdough
2026-07-26T02:45:25.518916863Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: we want this labeler to help both our current members, and potential newcomers
2026-07-26T02:45:25.518926364Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: this group is about naturally-leavened, from-scratch baking. home-milled flour, wild starter, the slow way
2026-07-26T02:45:25.518961196Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: we want this moderation service to help newcomers and existing members alike
2026-07-26T02:45:25.519002168Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [ai]: [{'text': 'Perfect! A home baking community focused on naturally-leavened bread, home-milled flour, and the slow, from-scratch approach. That\'s beautifully specific.\n\nNow let\'s define the labels — the categories you want to flag and how each should be handled:\n\n**1. Posts that embody your "from-scratch" ethos** (naturally-leavened, home-milled, slow baking)\n   - How should these be marked? Just a positive/informational label that stays visible on the post so people can spot the good examples? Or something else?\n\n**2. Drive-by product spam** that doesn\'t fit your culture\n   - How should these be handled? Should they be hidden behind a click-through warning, or just carry a warning label while staying visible, or something else?\n\nOnce I know how you want each category treated, I\'ll design the complete labeler configuration for your approval.', 'type': 'text', 'index': 0}]
