2026-07-26T02:51:01.743050112Z INFO:src.api.chatbot:→ node: agent
2026-07-26T02:51:01.749032072Z INFO:src.api.chatbot:  llm call: agent
2026-07-26T02:51:02.851549579Z INFO:httpx:HTTP Request: POST https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages "HTTP/1.1 200 OK"
2026-07-26T02:51:08.464298067Z INFO:src.api.chatbot:→ node: agent
2026-07-26T02:51:08.476802038Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: hey y'all
2026-07-26T02:51:08.476953686Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: okay we've put this off long enough. we keep saying our community has a certain way of doing things, and new folks have no way of knowing what that is. let's actually encode it.
2026-07-26T02:51:08.477043001Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: agreed, but carefully. I want this to help people understand our norms, not slap a scarlet letter on everyone who's new.
2026-07-26T02:51:08.477128376Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: two things I'd want marked. posts that fit our "from-scratch" ethos so people can find the good stuff. And the drive-by product spam that has nothing to do with our culture.
2026-07-26T02:51:08.477176068Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: yeah those are the two. one's a positive marker, one's a "this isn't us" marker.
2026-07-26T02:51:08.477284134Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: @CLEO can we get started?
2026-07-26T02:51:08.517079583Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [ai]: [{'text': 'Absolutely! Let\'s get started. I need to understand a bit more about your labeler\'s purpose before we design the labels.\n\n**What community is this for, and who\'s the intended audience?** \n\nI\'m picking up that you have a "from-scratch ethos" and want to help newcomers understand your norms while flagging product spam that doesn\'t fit your culture. But I need to know:\n\n- What kind of community is this? (e.g., a crafting community, a cooking community, a DIY/maker space, a gardening group?)\n- Who will subscribe to this labeler — just your community members, or are you hoping to help a broader audience find content that aligns with these values?\n\nThis context will help me design labels that truly serve your moderation goal and speak to your audience in the right way.', 'type': 'text', 'index': 0}]
2026-07-26T02:51:08.517103334Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: we're a home baking community of about 300 people on bluesky
2026-07-26T02:51:08.517108994Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: yea, our content is cnetered on home milling, naturally-leavened bread
2026-07-26T02:51:08.517122765Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: and sourdough
2026-07-26T02:51:08.517742149Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: we want this labeler to help both our current members, and potential newcomers
2026-07-26T02:51:08.5177533Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: this group is about naturally-leavened, from-scratch baking. home-milled flour, wild starter, the slow way
2026-07-26T02:51:08.51775719Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: we want this moderation service to help newcomers and existing members alike
2026-07-26T02:51:08.51776259Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [ai]: [{'text': 'Perfect! A home baking community focused on naturally-leavened bread, home-milled flour, and the slow, from-scratch approach. That\'s beautifully specific.\n\nNow let\'s define the labels — the categories you want to flag and how each should be handled:\n\n**1. Posts that embody your "from-scratch" ethos** (naturally-leavened, home-milled, slow baking)\n   - How should these be marked? Just a positive/informational label that stays visible on the post so people can spot the good examples? Or something else?\n\n**2. Drive-by product spam** that doesn\'t fit your culture\n   - How should these be handled? Should they be hidden behind a click-through warning, or just carry a warning label while staying visible, or something else?\n\nOnce I know how you want each category treated, I\'ll design the complete labeler configuration for your approval.', 'type': 'text', 'index': 0}]
2026-07-26T02:51:08.517768001Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: the from-scratch one should just be a visible badge. it's a signal, a little "this exemplifies our values" marker. nothing hidden, obviously. we want people to see it.
2026-07-26T02:51:08.517772001Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: definitely visible. it's a badge of belonging, not a warning.
2026-07-26T02:51:08.517776721Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: the second thing is the dropshipper spam. accounts show up posting "PROFESSIONAL DUTCH OVEN 60% OFF LINK IN BIO," "DM me for artisan banneton wholesale". brand-new accounts blasting product links. that's the opposite of our culture. it's not against a safety rule, it's just categorically not what this community is.
2026-07-26T02:51:08.517788822Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: hide the out-of-bounds spam fully. it's categorically not us, nobody needs it in the feed. bury it behind a click-through.
2026-07-26T02:51:08.517792212Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: yeah, hide the spam
2026-07-26T02:51:08.517795652Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: works for me
2026-07-26T02:51:08.517800542Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [ai]: [{'text': "Perfect! I've got everything I need. Let me stage the complete labeler configuration for your approval:\n\n**Two labels:**\n1. **From-scratch badge** — a visible, positive marker for posts that exemplify your naturally-leavened, home-milled, slow-baking values\n2. **Product spam filter** — hides drive-by dropshipper posts (professional equipment sales, wholesale pitches, link-in-bio spam) behind a click-through so your feed stays focused on your culture\n\nLet me finalize this now:", 'type': 'text', 'index': 0}, {'id': 'toolu_01SnG6EPdNUxacErjQ26UbFx', 'input': {}, 'name': 'finalize_proposal', 'type': 'tool_use', 'caller': {'type': 'direct'}, 'index': 1, 'partial_json': '{"display_name": "From-Scratch Baking Community", "description": "A moderation service for the home baking community focused on naturally-leavened bread, home-milled flour, and slow, from-scratch methods. Highlights posts that embody these values and filters out product spam.", "labels": [{"identifier":"from_scratch_baking","severity":"inform","blurs":"none","locales":[{"lang":"en","name":"From-Scratch Baking","description":"Content that exemplifies naturally-leavened, home-milled, slow-baking values"}]},{"identifier":"product_spam","severity":"inform","blurs":"content","locales":[{"lang":"en","name":"Product Spam","description":"Drive-by product promotion unrelated to from-scratch baking culture"}]}]}'}]
2026-07-26T02:51:08.51847633Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [tool]: Proposal staged successfully.
2026-07-26T02:51:08.518495171Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [ai]: [{'text': '**✓ Configuration staged for approval!**\n\nYour labeler now has:\n\n1. **From-Scratch Baking** — A visible badge (no hiding, just an informational label) for posts that exemplify your naturally-leavened, home-milled, slow-baking ethos. Members and newcomers can spot the good examples at a glance.\n\n2. **Product Spam** — Hides drive-by dropshipper posts behind a click-through. When someone posts "PROFESSIONAL DUTCH OVEN 60% OFF" or wholesale banneton pitches, subscribers won\'t see it in their feed unless they choose to click through.\n\n**What\'s next:** The group will review and approve this configuration. Once approved, you\'ll move on to defining the *classification rules* — the specific signals (keywords, patterns, account traits) that determine which posts get which label. That\'s where you\'ll specify things like "brand-new accounts posting product links" or the markers of authentic from-scratch content.', 'type': 'text', 'index': 0}]
