2026-07-26T02:57:26.064358395Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: and sourdough
2026-07-26T02:57:26.064378086Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: we want this labeler to help both our current members, and potential newcomers
2026-07-26T02:57:26.064384527Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: this group is about naturally-leavened, from-scratch baking. home-milled flour, wild starter, the slow way
2026-07-26T02:57:26.064402178Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: we want this moderation service to help newcomers and existing members alike
2026-07-26T02:57:26.064430299Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [ai]: [{'text': 'Perfect! A home baking community focused on naturally-leavened bread, home-milled flour, and the slow, from-scratch approach. That\'s beautifully specific.\n\nNow let\'s define the labels — the categories you want to flag and how each should be handled:\n\n**1. Posts that embody your "from-scratch" ethos** (naturally-leavened, home-milled, slow baking)\n   - How should these be marked? Just a positive/informational label that stays visible on the post so people can spot the good examples? Or something else?\n\n**2. Drive-by product spam** that doesn\'t fit your culture\n   - How should these be handled? Should they be hidden behind a click-through warning, or just carry a warning label while staying visible, or something else?\n\nOnce I know how you want each category treated, I\'ll design the complete labeler configuration for your approval.', 'type': 'text', 'index': 0}]
2026-07-26T02:57:26.06444309Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: the from-scratch one should just be a visible badge. it's a signal, a little "this exemplifies our values" marker. nothing hidden, obviously. we want people to see it.
2026-07-26T02:57:26.064539565Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: definitely visible. it's a badge of belonging, not a warning.
2026-07-26T02:57:26.064549736Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: the second thing is the dropshipper spam. accounts show up posting "PROFESSIONAL DUTCH OVEN 60% OFF LINK IN BIO," "DM me for artisan banneton wholesale". brand-new accounts blasting product links. that's the opposite of our culture. it's not against a safety rule, it's just categorically not what this community is.
2026-07-26T02:57:26.064591268Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: hide the out-of-bounds spam fully. it's categorically not us, nobody needs it in the feed. bury it behind a click-through.
2026-07-26T02:57:26.06461946Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: yeah, hide the spam
2026-07-26T02:57:26.064668032Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: works for me
2026-07-26T02:57:26.064694494Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [ai]: [{'text': '**✓ Configuration staged for approval!**\n\nYour labeler now has:\n\n1. **From-Scratch Baking** — A visible badge (no hiding, just an informational label) for posts that exemplify your naturally-leavened, home-milled, slow-baking ethos. Members and newcomers can spot the good examples at a glance.\n\n2. **Product Spam** — Hides drive-by dropshipper posts behind a click-through. When someone posts "PROFESSIONAL DUTCH OVEN 60% OFF" or wholesale banneton pitches, subscribers won\'t see it in their feed unless they choose to click through.\n\n**What\'s next:** The group will review and approve this configuration. Once approved, you\'ll move on to defining the *classification rules* — the specific signals (keywords, patterns, account traits) that determine which posts get which label. That\'s where you\'ll specify things like "brand-new accounts posting product links" or the markers of authentic from-scratch content.', 'type': 'text', 'index': 0}]
2026-07-26T02:57:26.064766288Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: [Group decision: the labeler configuration you staged were put to a vote and APPROVED. They are now committed and are the current labeler configuration shown in your system prompt. This is done — do not ask the group to approve them again, and do not re-stage them unchanged.]
2026-07-26T02:57:26.064775098Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: perf
2026-07-26T02:57:26.064826231Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: the vocabulary is pretty consistent for the from-scratch marker. "wild yeast," "naturally leavened," "home-milled," "fresh-milled flour," "levain," "no commercial yeast," "100% whole grain," that kind of language. people describing the slow process.
2026-07-26T02:57:26.064845972Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: "starter" and "sourdough" alone are too broad
2026-07-26T02:57:26.064885874Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: everyone says those. it's the from-scratch vocabulary that marks the real thing.
2026-07-26T02:57:26.064901345Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: and please, this is a positive label, so worst case it's just missing from a post that deserved it. I'd rather it under-mark than slap the badge on something ironically. keep it to the genuine from-scratch language
2026-07-26T02:57:26.064935017Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: that's right. cleo, keep it to the real from-scratch vocabulary.
2026-07-26T02:57:26.06498955Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [ai]: [{'text': 'Got it. For the **From-Scratch Baking** label, I\'ll catch posts that use the genuine from-scratch vocabulary — "wild yeast," "naturally leavened," "home-milled," "fresh-milled flour," "levain," "no commercial yeast," "100% whole grain" — the language that signals someone is actually doing the slow, from-scratch work.\n\nI\'ll skip "starter" and "sourdough" alone since everyone uses those. This way the badge only appears on posts that truly exemplify your values, not on every casual mention.\n\n**Now for the Product Spam label** — what should I look for to catch those drive-by dropshipper posts? You mentioned brand-new accounts posting things like "PROFESSIONAL DUTCH OVEN 60% OFF LINK IN BIO" or "DM me for artisan banneton wholesale."\n\nShould I flag:\n- Product/sales language (discount codes, "link in bio," "DM me," wholesale pitches) from brand-new accounts?\n- Any other signals that mark the drive-by spam as distinct from a community member occasionally mentioning a tool they like?\n\nWhat makes it spam versus a genuine recommendation in your community?', 'type': 'text', 'index': 0}]
2026-07-26T02:57:26.064999341Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: now the out-of-community spam. same tell every time: a product-pitch phrase plus it's a brand-new account with basically no followers. "link in bio," "DM for wholesale," "60% off," "limited stock", plus a follower count near zero. actual members who mention a link have hundreds of followers. it's the combination that marks it as not-us.
2026-07-26T02:57:26.065037953Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: yeah, the combination feels safe. an established member sharing a link won't get caught because they've got followers.
2026-07-26T02:57:26.065062404Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [human]: so it's the sales phrase AND the low follower count together. either alone would catch real people
2026-07-26T02:57:26.065157219Z INFO:src.agent.brainstorming.nodes:feedback graph message [ai]: [{'text': 'Perfect — so **Product Spam** fires when a post has BOTH:\n- Sales/promo language ("link in bio," "DM for wholesale," "60% off," "limited stock," etc.)\n- AND it\'s from a brand-new account with very low followers (basically zero)\n\nEither signal alone would catch real community members, but together they mark the drive-by dropshippers who aren\'t part of your culture.\n\n---\n\n**Here are the complete rules for both labels:**\n\n**From-Scratch Baking** will catch posts using genuine from-scratch vocabulary — "wild yeast," "naturally leavened," "home-milled," "fresh-milled flour," "levain," "no commercial yeast," "100% whole grain." It skips broad terms like "starter" or "sourdough" alone, so the badge only appears on posts that truly exemplify your slow, from-scratch values.\n\n**Product Spam** will catch posts that combine sales pitches ("link in bio," "DM me," discount percentages, "limited stock," "wholesale") with very low follower counts (10 or fewer). Established members sharing a link won\'t be flagged because they have followers; it\'s the combination that marks the drive-by spam.\n\nI\'ve staged these rules — react 👍🏾 to approve, or just tell me what to change.', 'type': 'text', 'index': 0}, {'id': 'toolu_01DzRJmdmPFUeXs69mXPeTyn', 'input': {}, 'name': 'finalize_rules', 'type': 'tool_use', 'caller': {'type': 'direct'}, 'index': 1, 'partial_json': '{"rules": [{"label_identifier":"from_scratch_baking","include_groups":[{"all_of":[{"type":"pattern","value":"\\\\b(wild yeast|naturally leavened|naturally-leavened|home-milled|home milled|fresh-milled|fresh milled|levain|no commercial yeast|100% whole grain)\\\\b","plain_name":"from-scratch baking vocabulary"}]}],"exclude_signals":[],"notes":"Catches posts using genuine from-scratch vocabulary like \'wild yeast,\' \'naturally leavened,\' \'home-milled,\' \'fresh-milled flour,\' \'levain,\' \'no commercial yeast,\' or \'100% whole grain.\' Skips broad terms like \'starter\' or \'sourdough\' alone so the badge only appears on posts that truly exemplify slow, from-scratch values."},{"label_identifier":"product_spam","include_groups":[{"all_of":[{"type":"pattern","value":"\\\\b(link in bio|dm (me|for)|\\\\d+%\\\\s*off|limited stock|wholesale|discount code|promo code|shop now|buy now|order now)\\\\b","plain_name":"sales or promo language"},{"type":"account","value":"follower_count <= 10","plain_name":"brand-new account with very few followers"}]}],"exclude_signals":[],"notes":"Catches posts combining sales pitches (link in bio, DM me, discount percentages, limited stock, wholesale) with very low follower counts (10 or fewer). Established members sharing a link won\'t be flagged because they have followers; it\'s the combination that marks drive-by dropshipper spam."}]}'}]
